\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:<a href=\"https://docs.tscircuit.com/llms.txt\">llms.txt</a>\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:  <a href=\"https://console.algora.io/org/tscircuit/bounties?status=completed\">\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:       <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Fconsole.algora.io%2Fapi%2Fshields%2Ftscircuit%2Fbounties%3Fstatus%3Dcompleted\" alt=\"Rewarded Bounties\">\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:   <a href=\"https://console.algora.io/org/tscircuit/bounties?status=open\">\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:       <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Fconsole.algora.io%2Fapi%2Fshields%2Ftscircuit%2Fbounties%3Fstatus%3Dopen\" alt=\"Open Bounties\">\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:  <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://tscircuit.com/join\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Discord-tscircuit.com/join-%235865F2\" alt=\"Join TSCircuit on Discord\"></a>\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:  <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/tscircuit\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/tscircuit\" alt=\"NPM Version\"></a>\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:  <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/stargazers\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/stars/tscircuit/tscircuit\" alt=\"GitHub Stars\"></a>\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:1. [What is tscircuit?](#about-tscircuit)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:## What is tscircuit?\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:`tscircuit` is a library complemented by a registry, package manager, command line tool and AI electronic design suite that makes it easy to create, share, export and manufacture electronic circuits. It uses\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:Think of tscircuit as \"React for Electronics\" It allows you to design real-world electronic circuits using Typescript and React. This is what tscircuit code looks like, instead of creating web element like “div”, you create circuit elements like “chip”, “resistor” or “capacitor”, then instead of rendering a website, we render a 3d circuit (that you can actually order!)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:Using tscircuit, you can design things like a <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://blog.tscircuit.com/p/battling-jlcs-assembly-interface\" target=\"_blank\">fully functional keyboard!</a> Once you've completed your design, you can export it to a manufacturer and order a real, functional circuit board!\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [ESP32 Wifi Breakout Board](https://tscircuit.com/seveibar/wifi-test-board-1)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:You can do everything you need to do with `tscircuit` using the [`tsci`](https://github.com/tscircuit/cli) command line tool.\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:npm install -g tscircuit\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:tsci dev\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:> ![tsci Server Preview](./docs/example_preview.png)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [x] Add [registry packages](https://tscircuit.com/) with `tsci add`\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [x] Publish subpackages to the registry with `tsci push`\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [x] Generate footprints from text [using AI](https://text-to-footprint.tscircuit.com)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:### Is tscircuit free?\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:tscircuit is completely free and MIT-licensed open-source\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:tscircuit uses the same thing that React Native and [react-three-fiber](https://docs.pmnd.rs/react-three-fiber/getting-started/introduction) use to render to mobile or 3d to render PCBs and schematics (it's called [React Fiber](https://github.com/acdlite/react-fiber-architecture)!)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:import { Schematic } from \"@tscircuit/schematic-viewer\"\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:tscircuit has a bunch of extra tools and exports in the command line, so it's a bit easier to use `tsci dev` to develop circuits (you can always publish and import them later)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:Yes! There is a [playground tool!](https://tscircuit.com/editor)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:Please [create an issue](https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues)!\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [@seveibar](https://x.com/seveibar) is the main author, he tweets about tscircuit and does [development livestreams](https://www.twitch.tv/seveibar)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [@tscircuit](https://x.com/tscircuit) for major tscircuit releases, features and discussions\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [tscircuit discord](https://discord.gg/6X3PYhtj) and [tscircuit campfire](https://tscircuit.com/community/join-redirect)\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:tscircuit includes a lot of different independently-runnable sub-projects. Here's\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [tscircuit](https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit)                          | The main package, packages up everything into a single version                                           |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/core](https://github.com/tscircuit/core)                         | A typescript-native library for building circuits (no React). Converts typescript into \"the circuit-json format\" |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/cli](https://github.com/tscircuit/cli)                           | The tscircuit command line tool `tsci` and development environment                                       |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/tscircuit.com](https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit.com)       | The main website, playground and online development environment for tscircuit                            |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/schematic-viewer](https://github.com/tscircuit/schematic-viewer) | The Schematic renderer                                                                                   |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/pcb-viewer](https://github.com/tscircuit/pcb-viewer)             | The PCB renderer                                                                                         |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/react-fiber](https://github.com/tscircuit/react-fiber)           | Bindings from builder to React, React types                                                              |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/routing](https://github.com/tscircuit/routing)                   | Routing algorithms for schematic and PCB traces                                                          |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/autolayout](https://github.com/tscircuit/autolayout)             | Layout algorithms for schematics                                                                         |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/footprinter](https://github.com/tscircuit/footprinter)           | DSL for creating footprints                                                                              |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [kicad-mod-converter](https://github.com/tscircuit/kicad-mod-converter)      | Convert kicad_mod files to and from JSON                                                                 |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:| [@tscircuit/kicad-viewer](https://github.com/tscircuit/kicad-viewer)         | View the KiCad official footprints online                                                                |\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [tscircuit.com](https://tscircuit.com/) - The official tscircuit website, registry and playground\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [discord](https://tscircuit.com/community/join-redirect) - Join the community server where all the primary conversations happen\nnode_modules/tscircuit/README.md:- [@seveibar](https://x.com/seveibar) - Twitter for author of tscircuit with dev sessions and upcoming features\nnode_modules/@tscircuit/cli/README.md:# tscircuit command line interface (CLI)\nnode