[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0f813c796c52cddb016a35af26f77c8197beae2128c6f8f593","text":"Implemented the schematic-only tscircuit test in [ring-light.circuit.tsx](/workspace/ring-light.circuit.tsx:1).\n\nWhat’s included:\n- USB-C PD input modeled around STUSB4500-style sink control.\n- LM3409 LED buck driver section with switch node, sense resistor, boot cap, COFF timing, OVP divider.\n- Flicker-free dimming control nets: `DIM_PWM` and `IADJ_DAC`.\n- Ring LED output connector plus warm/cool LED segment placeholders.\n- `routingDisabled` enabled.\n- No tscircuit registry components used; only built-in primitives plus JLCPCB metadata on passives/commodity parts.\n\nValidation run:\n- `npm run check` passed.\n- `npx tsci check schematic-placement ring-light.circuit.tsx` passed with no placement issues.\n- `npm run build` passed. It still emits non-blocking pin-attribute warnings for generic chip symbols, plus LED supplier-footprint warnings from built-in LED defaults.\n- `npm run snapshot` passed; snapshots are in [__snapshots__](/workspace/__snapshots__/ring-light.circuit-schematic.snap.svg).\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n- Confusing/surprising: the skill example used `schematicsection`, `connector`, `schSectionName`, and `schDisplayValue`, but the initially installed tscircuit typings rejected several of those APIs. Updating packages changed available behavior.\n- Most time wasted: resolving CLI/runtime dependency skew. The global CLI and local package versions disagreed, then the local CLI exposed multiple missing or stale dependencies before `schematic-placement` would run.\n- Helpful changes: a single pinned working `tscircuit` starter template, clearer compatibility matrix for `tsci`/`@tscircuit/core`/`@tscircuit/eval`, and a checker command that reports version mismatch directly.\n- Specific friction: schematic placement required repeated exact-coordinate edits; JLCPCB supplier metadata can create noisy footprint mismatch warnings when the schematic intentionally uses placeholder built-in footprints.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019ee1a7-4e8c-7d90-ba3a-cc7701bc621e","turnId":"019ee1a7-4ebd-7272-aad1-4378370a8876","completedAtMs":1781903156556}}
